  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urgent support and protection for at-risk older women and men in Ukraine, Poland and Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cash distributed in Ukraine and Moldova to at-risk older women and men with and without disabilities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hygiene Kits and Assistive products, and COVID kits are distributed among targeted individuals as required</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved access to basic essential goods and services through conditional cash assistance for at-risk older women and men with and without disabilities within Ukraine and refugees in Moldova</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased access to inclusive, protection-based humanitarian support that contributes to their improved security, dignity, and wellbeing for at-risk older women and men with and without disabilities within Ukraine and refugees in Moldova</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outreach programme of support visits to provide basic social care services for homebound older people in their homes or wherever they have been displaced (including collective centres in Moldova)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Referral support to existing functional health care and other services for homebound older people is established</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase access to inclusive, protection-based humanitarian support that contributes to their improved security, dignity, and wellbeing for at-risk older women and men with and without disabilities within Ukraine and refugees in Moldova</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training provided to build the capacity of service providers and collective centres to ensure they are inclusive of older women and men with and without disabilities</narrative>
  </description>
